Simpleton: one open SACD/DFF/DVD-A container per thread, not per process

The sacdiso, dsdiff and dvdaiso plugins (patch 0001) keep the container
they have open - path, media, reader - in plugin-wide globals, shared by
every thread that calls into the plugin: the decoder thread playing a
track, the update thread scanning the library, the client thread reading
tags. A library scan while a track from an ISO plays (or sits restored-
paused after a restart: restore_paused "yes") reopens the globals under
the decoder, which then reads frames from a disc with no track selected
and MPD dies with SIGSEGV. Seen on the unit 11 Oct (an MPD restart while
a DST track played), 26 Oct, and 28 Oct 2026 four times in 70 s after a
DAC swap (the hotplug restart + the card rescan that followed it).

thread_local on the three plugins' container state gives each thread its
own open container. Every entry point (container_scan, file_decode,
scan_file) already opens through container_update() on the calling
thread, so nothing else changes; a thread's container is closed when the
thread ends (the update threads are per job).

diff --git a/src/decoder/plugins/DffDecoderPlugin.cxx b/src/decoder/plugins/DffDecoderPlugin.cxx
index 6810d3c..23eaa39 100644
--- a/src/decoder/plugins/DffDecoderPlugin.cxx
+++ b/src/decoder/plugins/DffDecoderPlugin.cxx
@@ -57,9 +57,13 @@ bool      param_lsbitfirst;
 area_id_e param_playable_area;
 bool      param_use_stdio;
 
-AllocatedPath                  dsdiff_path{ nullptr };
-std::unique_ptr<sacd_media_t>  sacd_media;
-std::unique_ptr<sacd_reader_t> sacd_reader;
+/* thread_local (Simpleton 0007, 29 Oct 2026): the decoder thread, the
+ * update thread and the client thread each keep their own open container.
+ * Shared, a library scan reopened the container under a playing (or
+ * restored-paused) decoder and MPD crashed with SIGSEGV. */
+thread_local AllocatedPath                  dsdiff_path{ nullptr };
+thread_local std::unique_ptr<sacd_media_t>  sacd_media;
+thread_local std::unique_ptr<sacd_reader_t> sacd_reader;
 
 static unsigned
 get_subsong(Path path_fs) {
